<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Oct 1.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Oct 1.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF OCTOBER 1 VERSUS SEPTEMBER 24, 1996	    DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   13/36    1/2     228/178  109/133  351/349    206</p>
<p> SASK.	6/3     0/0	63/60     7/14    76/77	45</p>
<p> B.C.	 1/4     0/0	18/13    16/18    35/35	10</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	2/2	4/4	  0</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 1/1	0/0	1/1	  0</p>
<p> TOTAL     20/43    1/2     312/254  134/167  467/466    261</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
